    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d108">

                <pb facs="0337" n="309" xml:id="pg309"/>

                <head>108. Memorandum by the Secretary of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d108-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1955-07-05"><hi rendition="#italic">July 5,
                        1955</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I read Mr. Merchant’s memorandum on US
                    Policy towards proposed European Atomic Pool.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d108-f2"/> I
                    have also read Mr. Smith’s dissent from
                    Mr. Merchant’s recommendations.<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d108-f3"/></p>
                <p>I agree with recommendations (1) and (2). I agree with (3a), with emphasis on
                    “assist Belgium”. I do not think we should pressure Belgium.</p>
                <p>With reference to (3b), I do not think we should use delay as a means of
                    coercion. I do not think we should rush these other bilateral arrangements but
                    should go ahead in an orderly way with the understanding that if the pool is
                    agreed upon, we should treat them in the same way as we treat the Belgian
                    agreement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >JFD</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
